1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,900
You don't need to be happy every day for

2
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:05,240
a happy life.

3
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:07,320
Maybe it's a strange idea,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,100
but I'd like you to think about it for a moment.

5
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:11,540
Hello, my friend.

6
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:13,380
Welcome to Cozy French Radio.

7
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:15,590
It's Lia, and I'm really happy to spend

8
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:17,660
this moment with you.

9
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,840
How do you feel today?

10
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:22,030
Did your day start well?

11
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:24,240
Or do you already have a lot of things

12
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,340
on your mind?

13
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:27,070
Maybe you're tired.

14
00:00:27,070 --> 00:00:29,710
Maybe something is worrying you.

15
00:00:29,710 --> 00:00:31,600
Or maybe everything is fine,

16
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:34,030
but you don't really know why you

17
00:00:34,030 --> 00:00:35,360
feel a little sad.

18
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:38,310
You know, sometimes we don't even have a clear reason

19
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:40,750
to be in a bad mood.

20
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:42,240
And that's okay.

21
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:44,760
Earlier, while preparing this episode,

22
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:46,150
I opened my window.

23
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:47,610
The sky was grey.

24
00:00:47,610 --> 00:00:49,550
There wasn't much light,

25
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:52,800
but I heard a bird singing somewhere in the street.

26
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:53,580
I smiled.

27
00:00:53,580 --> 00:00:56,140
Not because this day was perfect.

28
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:59,060
Just because, for a few seconds,

29
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,880
I noticed something pleasant.

30
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:04,600
And it reminded me of something important.

31
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:08,060
A day doesn't need to be perfect to hold

32
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:09,300
a beautiful moment.

33
00:01:09,300 --> 00:01:12,530
Today, we're going to talk about positive thinking,

34
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:15,050
and above all about how to stay positive in

35
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:16,600
our everyday life.

36
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:18,460
And during this conversation,

37
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:21,150
you can also practise your French gently,

38
00:01:21,150 --> 00:01:24,500
with simple sentences and familiar situations.

39
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:27,300
You don't need to understand every word.

40
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:32,300
Just listen calmly, as if we were sitting together over a coffee.

41
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:35,100
Now, imagine this situation.

42
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:37,710
Someone wakes up on a Monday morning.

43
00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:39,180
Their alarm didn't go off.

44
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,700
They're late.

45
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:42,190
While making coffee,

46
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:44,740
they spill a little milk on the table.

47
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:48,000
Then, on the way out, they find out it's raining.

48
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,070
They look at the sky and think:

49
00:01:50,070 --> 00:01:52,100
"What a horrible day!"

50
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:54,800
And yet, it's only eight in the morning.

51
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:57,200
The day has barely started.

52
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,460
But in their head,

53
00:01:58,460 --> 00:01:59,940
everything is already decided.

54
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:02,100
It's going to be a bad day.

55
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:04,540
Have you ever lived something like that?

56
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:06,220
One small problem happens,

57
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:08,050
then another, and suddenly,

58
00:02:08,050 --> 00:02:10,700
we feel like everything is going wrong.

59
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:11,960
It's very human.

60
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:15,700
Our mind easily notices what isn't working.

61
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:18,450
But here's what we sometimes forget.

62
00:02:18,450 --> 00:02:22,300
A bad moment doesn't mean a bad day.

63
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:26,400
And a bad day doesn't mean a bad life.

64
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:29,140
Being positive isn't looking at the rain and

65
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:30,690
pretending the weather is nice.

66
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:32,600
It's admitting that it's raining,

67
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:35,800
taking an umbrella and getting on with your day.

68
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:37,360
Do you see the difference?

69
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:41,000
Positive thinking isn't an obligation to smile.

70
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:46,100
It's a way of looking at difficulties without forgetting the possibilities.

71
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:49,200
You can be sad and still have hope.

72
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:53,400
You can be tired and enjoy a small moment of calm.

73
00:02:53,420 --> 00:02:56,620
You can have problems and admit that there are

74
00:02:56,620 --> 00:02:59,100
still good things around you.

75
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:02,670
So, if today you don't feel particularly

76
00:03:02,670 --> 00:03:04,500
happy, don't judge yourself.

77
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:05,940
You haven't failed.

78
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:07,700
You're simply human.

79
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:10,850
And sometimes, the first step to becoming more positive

80
00:03:10,850 --> 00:03:13,680
is to stop asking ourselves why we aren't

81
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,400
happy all the time.

82
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:18,350
There's a little voice in our head

83
00:03:18,350 --> 00:03:21,660
that talks almost all day long.

84
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:24,800
Sometimes, it encourages us.

85
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:29,500
But sometimes, it tells stories that make us suffer.

86
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:31,050
And the strangest thing

87
00:03:31,050 --> 00:03:35,200
is that we often believe everything it says.

88
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:37,200
Imagine a very simple scene.

89
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,200
You send a message to a friend.

90
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:39,790
"Hi!

91
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:41,000
How are you?

92
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,800
Are you free this weekend?"

93
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,600
You wait for an answer.

94
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,090
An hour goes by.

95
00:03:46,090 --> 00:03:47,800
Then two hours.

96
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:50,600
Your phone stays silent.

97
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:52,740
At first, you don't worry.

98
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:57,700
But little by little, your mind starts inventing explanations.

99
00:03:57,700 --> 00:04:00,450
"Maybe he doesn't want to talk to me anymore."

100
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:03,200
"Did I say something wrong?"

101
00:04:03,200 --> 00:04:06,000
"He must be angry with me."

102
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,830
And now, you feel sad.

103
00:04:08,830 --> 00:04:11,400
Maybe even a little rejected.

104
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:13,760
And yet, what do you really know?

105
00:04:13,760 --> 00:04:17,180
You only know your friend hasn't replied yet.

106
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:18,300
That's all.

107
00:04:18,350 --> 00:04:20,020
Maybe he's working.

108
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:20,620
He's sleeping.

109
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:22,390
He forgot his phone.

110
00:04:22,390 --> 00:04:25,900
Or he's going through a hard day himself.

111
00:04:25,900 --> 00:04:29,770
But your mind chose a negative explanation.

112
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:33,200
And your emotion followed that explanation.

113
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:36,000
Fascinating, don't you think?

114
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,760
Sometimes, we don't suffer only because of

115
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:39,800
what happens.

116
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:42,720
We also suffer because of what we

117
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,500
imagine about what happens.

118
00:04:45,550 --> 00:04:48,600
Of course, some worries are real.

119
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:53,400
And sometimes, our intuition tells us a problem deserves our attention.

120
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:57,400
But a thought isn't automatically a fact.

121
00:04:57,400 --> 00:05:00,300
Here's a simple sentence you can use:

122
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:03,900
"I think this, but I don't know if it's true."

123
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:05,800
It seems small, this sentence.

124
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:09,600
But it can create a lot of space in our mind.

125
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,500
Let's take another example.

126
00:05:11,550 --> 00:05:13,390
You make a mistake at work.

127
00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:15,720
You forget an important detail.

128
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:17,000
And right away, you think:

129
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,690
"I'm really useless.

130
00:05:18,690 --> 00:05:21,100
I always make mistakes."

131
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,300
Always?

132
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:24,600
Really always?

133
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,000
Probably not.

134
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,200
Maybe you got a lot of things right this week.

135
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,630
Maybe you helped a colleague,

136
00:05:31,630 --> 00:05:34,600
finished a project or solved a problem.

137
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:38,440
But your mind only looks at this mistake.

138
00:05:38,490 --> 00:05:40,110
So, instead of saying:

139
00:05:40,110 --> 00:05:42,900
"I'm useless", you could think:

140
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:44,400
"I made a mistake.

141
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:47,100
I can try to fix it."

142
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:48,700
It's not a magic sentence.

143
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:51,200
It doesn't make the problem disappear.

144
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:54,300
But it changes the way you talk to yourself.

145
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:58,300
And the way you talk to yourself matters.

146
00:05:58,300 --> 00:06:01,000
Imagine your best friend makes a mistake.

147
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,500
Would you tell them:

148
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:06,340
"You're hopeless, you'll never succeed at anything"?

149
00:06:06,390 --> 00:06:07,890
No, probably not.

150
00:06:07,890 --> 00:06:09,800
You'd try to help them.

151
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:13,800
So why talk to yourself with less kindness?

152
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:18,180
Being positive doesn't mean replacing every negative thought

153
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:19,700
with a wonderful sentence.

154
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:21,140
It's not about saying:

155
00:06:21,140 --> 00:06:22,440
"Everything is perfect!"

156
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,000
when it isn't true.

157
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,300
It's more about looking for a fairer thought.

158
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:31,600
A thought that admits the difficulty without condemning you.

159
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:35,100
"It's hard, but I can learn."

160
00:06:35,150 --> 00:06:39,600
"I'm worried, but I don't have all the information yet."

161
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,700
"Today, I didn't succeed,

162
00:06:41,700 --> 00:06:44,700
but that doesn't define my whole life."

163
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:45,300
You see?

164
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:48,250
You don't have to believe all the stories

165
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:49,700
your mind tells.

166
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:53,960
Sometimes, you just need to answer it gently: "Wait.

167
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:57,100
Let's look at the facts before deciding."

168
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:59,900
And this little pause can change your mood,

169
00:06:59,900 --> 00:07:03,440
your reaction and sometimes even your whole day.

170
00:07:03,490 --> 00:07:07,180
What if your life already held more happiness

171
00:07:07,180 --> 00:07:09,400
than you thought?

172
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:11,800
Not a spectacular happiness.

173
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:14,690
Not something that looks like an advert or

174
00:07:14,690 --> 00:07:16,600
a perfect photo.

175
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:20,450
I mean those little moments that go by so

176
00:07:20,450 --> 00:07:24,900
fast that we sometimes forget to notice them.

177
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:27,930
Imagine someone coming home after a

178
00:07:27,930 --> 00:07:29,600
long day at work.

179
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,400
She's tired.

180
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:34,500
On the metro, she looks at the other passengers.

181
00:07:34,500 --> 00:07:36,300
Everyone seems busy.

182
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:38,300
Some are looking at their phones.

183
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:40,500
Others close their eyes.

184
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:43,400
She thinks about everything she still has to do.

185
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,840
Make dinner.

186
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:46,500
Answer a few messages.

187
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,100
Tidy her flat.

188
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,400
Get her things ready for the next day.

189
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:55,700
In her head, the day is just a long list of responsibilities.

190
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:57,400
But when she gets home,

191
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,600
something happens.

192
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:00,840
She opens the door.

193
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:03,300
Her cat comes gently towards her.

194
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:07,600
It rubs against her legs and starts to purr.

195
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:10,800
For a few seconds, she forgets how tired she is.

196
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:12,300
She smiles.

197
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:15,500
This little moment doesn't change her responsibilities.

198
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:17,800
Dinner still has to be made.

199
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:20,100
The messages are still waiting.

200
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:22,200
But something has changed.

201
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:25,540
She has just felt a little joy.

202
00:08:25,590 --> 00:08:28,280
And that joy was already there,

203
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:31,700
in a very ordinary scene.

204
00:08:31,700 --> 00:08:33,980
You know, we often have this idea that

205
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:36,000
happiness has to come later.

206
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,900
When we have a better job.

207
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:39,800
When we earn more money.

208
00:08:39,800 --> 00:08:41,900
When we've finished our projects.

209
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:43,700
When we go on holiday.

210
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:46,800
When our life is finally simpler.

211
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:49,540
But what happens if we spend our whole

212
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:52,900
life waiting for the next happy event?

213
00:08:52,950 --> 00:08:55,450
We risk never really seeing what's

214
00:08:55,450 --> 00:08:57,000
right in front of us.

215
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,900
Of course, having dreams is a beautiful thing.

216
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:02,900
Wanting to improve your situation is normal.

217
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:05,770
But we can move towards a better future while

218
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:08,500
enjoying some moments of the present.

219
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,600
Both are possible.

220
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:13,530
You can want another life without hating the one

221
00:09:13,530 --> 00:09:15,100
you have today.

222
00:09:15,100 --> 00:09:19,500
You can have big ambitions and love the little things.

223
00:09:19,550 --> 00:09:22,340
Maybe your morning coffee tastes exactly

224
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:23,700
the way you like it.

225
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:27,000
Maybe a song reminds you of a lovely memory.

226
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,700
Maybe someone smiled at you in the street.

227
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:32,450
Maybe you managed to understand a French sentence

228
00:09:32,450 --> 00:09:35,900
you found difficult last week.

229
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:38,100
These aren't big events.

230
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:40,300
But they're real moments.

231
00:09:40,300 --> 00:09:43,600
And noticing them doesn't mean ignoring your problems.

232
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:47,320
It simply means also making room for

233
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:49,000
what's going well.

234
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:50,700
I really like this idea:

235
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:54,600
a day can hold several emotions at the same time.

236
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:57,900
You can be tired and grateful.

237
00:09:57,900 --> 00:10:01,600
You can be worried and laugh with someone.

238
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:06,300
You can have a hard day and enjoy a good meal.

239
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:09,050
We don't need to choose just one emotion

240
00:10:09,050 --> 00:10:11,300
for the whole day.

241
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:14,200
So, here's a little question.

242
00:10:14,200 --> 00:10:18,420
When did you last notice something pleasant?

243
00:10:18,470 --> 00:10:20,800
Not necessarily something extraordinary.

244
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:23,800
Just a moment that did you good.

245
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:25,300
Maybe this morning.

246
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:26,800
Maybe yesterday.

247
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:31,500
Or maybe now, while you're listening to this conversation.

248
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:33,800
Maybe you're in a quiet room.

249
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:36,500
Maybe you have a few minutes to yourself.

250
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:37,900
And during these minutes,

251
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:41,200
nobody is asking you to achieve anything.

252
00:10:41,200 --> 00:10:44,700
You can simply be here.

253
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:48,500
Sometimes, being positive starts with this ability.

254
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:51,200
Noticing what's already here.

255
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:53,100
Not to forget what's missing.

256
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:55,840
But so that what's missing doesn't hide

257
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:56,600
everything else.

258
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,900
You can have a free day…

259
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:02,500
and feel completely exhausted.

260
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:04,500
That may seem strange.

261
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:06,500
You didn't work much.

262
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,400
You didn't do any sport.

263
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:11,200
You didn't even leave your flat.

264
00:11:11,250 --> 00:11:13,740
And yet, in the evening,

265
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:15,500
you feel drained.

266
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,500
Why?

267
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:20,440
Because not all tiredness comes from

268
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,000
physical activity.

269
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Some comes from what we watch,

270
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:27,630
what we listen to and what

271
00:11:27,630 --> 00:11:31,000
we think about for hours.

272
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,500
Imagine a Sunday morning.

273
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:36,000
Someone wakes up slowly.

274
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,700
She has nothing urgent to do.

275
00:11:38,750 --> 00:11:42,000
She picks up her phone to look at a few photos.

276
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,500
At first, it's nice.

277
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,500
She sees friends,

278
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:48,000
trips, pretty houses.

279
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,500
Then she starts comparing.

280
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:53,000
A friend has just bought a flat.

281
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:56,000
A former colleague got a promotion.

282
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Someone shares holiday photos from a stunning place.

283
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,500
And slowly, a thought appears.

284
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:07,200
"Everyone is moving forward, except me."

285
00:12:07,250 --> 00:12:09,000
A few minutes earlier,

286
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
she was feeling pretty good.

287
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Now, she feels her life isn't interesting enough.

288
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:20,000
But has her life really changed in those twenty minutes?

289
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
No.

290
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
What has changed

291
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,500
is the way she looks at herself.

292
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:28,000
Maybe you recognise this feeling.

293
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,930
We sometimes compare our ordinary day to the

294
00:12:31,930 --> 00:12:34,140
most beautiful moments of other people's lives.

295
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:35,120
We see their success,

296
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:37,000
but rarely their doubts.

297
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:39,110
We see their smile,

298
00:12:39,110 --> 00:12:41,000
but not always their struggles.

299
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:44,000
And we forget something very simple.

300
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:48,000
We never know the whole story.

301
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
That doesn't mean social media is bad.

302
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
It can teach us a lot of things,

303
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
inspire us and bring us closer to others.

304
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,440
But it's useful to notice how we

305
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:02,200
feel after using it.

306
00:13:02,250 --> 00:13:05,000
Does this activity give me energy?

307
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Or does it leave me with a feeling of lack?

308
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:12,000
This question can also apply to some conversations.

309
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Maybe you know someone who constantly criticises everything.

310
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,000
The weather is bad.

311
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,000
Work is horrible.

312
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,990
People are unbearable.

313
00:13:20,990 --> 00:13:23,000
Nothing ever goes right.

314
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Of course, everyone has the right to talk about their problems.

315
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:31,000
And listening to someone who's hurting is a beautiful proof of friendship.

316
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:34,000
But there's a difference between supporting someone

317
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,000
and carrying all their emotions for them.

318
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,080
You can listen kindly without having to

319
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:43,000
solve every difficulty.

320
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:49,000
You can understand someone without automatically sharing all their negative thoughts.

321
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
And sometimes you can say:

322
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,000
"I'm a bit tired today.

323
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Can we talk about it tomorrow?"

324
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
That's not being selfish.

325
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,110
It's recognising your own limits.

326
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:03,000
Being positive doesn't require surrounding yourself only

327
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
with happy people.

328
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,570
It's more about paying attention to what

329
00:14:07,570 --> 00:14:09,000
feeds your mind.

330
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,200
Just as your body needs rest and

331
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:14,330
food, your mind needs moments when it

332
00:14:14,330 --> 00:14:17,000
isn't constantly being asked for something.

333
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Maybe a walk without your phone would do you good.

334
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:25,100
Maybe a simple chat with a friend could help you relax.

335
00:14:25,150 --> 00:14:28,410
Or maybe you just need a few

336
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:30,000
minutes of silence.

337
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:34,000
We talk a lot about organising our time well.

338
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
But we sometimes forget to protect our attention.

339
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,000
And yet, our attention is precious.

340
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,440
Because what we look at every day gently shapes

341
00:14:44,440 --> 00:14:47,000
the way we see our life.

342
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:50,740
And sometimes, finding a bit of positivity again doesn't

343
00:14:50,740 --> 00:14:53,140
require adding something.

344
00:14:53,190 --> 00:14:57,000
It simply requires making a little room.

345
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:00,000
There will be days when you do everything right…

346
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:04,000
and things still don't go as planned.

347
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
You'll get up on time.

348
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
You'll plan your day.

349
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
You'll try to stay calm.

350
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:14,000
And despite everything, a problem will come up.

351
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Maybe a cancelled appointment.

352
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Some bad news.

353
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,200
An unpleasant remark.

354
00:15:20,250 --> 00:15:24,000
Or just that tiredness that makes small difficulties

355
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,000
feel much bigger.

356
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,110
And in those moments,

357
00:15:27,110 --> 00:15:32,000
you might think: "But why is this happening to me again?"

358
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
I understand that reaction.

359
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
We'd all like to have a little more control

360
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,000
over our lives.

361
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,790
We'd like to know that if we make the right

362
00:15:40,790 --> 00:15:43,000
choices, everything will be fine.

363
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:47,200
But life doesn't always work that way.

364
00:15:47,250 --> 00:15:52,000
Imagine someone who has been planning a short trip for weeks.

365
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,210
She chose a lovely place,

366
00:15:54,210 --> 00:15:59,000
booked a room and pictured long walks in the sun.

367
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,440
But on the first day,

368
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:02,000
it pours with rain.

369
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
The sky is dark.

370
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
The streets are almost empty.

371
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
And she thinks:

372
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
"My holiday is ruined."

373
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,200
She stays in her room, disappointed.

374
00:16:13,250 --> 00:16:14,500
Then, after a while,

375
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:17,000
she decides to go out despite the rain.

376
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
She finds a quiet little café.

377
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
She orders a hot drink.

378
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,260
She sits by a window and watches the drops

379
00:16:24,260 --> 00:16:26,000
of water fall on the cobblestones.

380
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
It's not the day she had imagined.

381
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,000
But she discovers a kind of calm she didn't expect.

382
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
The holiday hasn't become perfect.

383
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
The rain is still there.

384
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:41,140
But the day has found another possibility.

385
00:16:41,190 --> 00:16:45,000
And sometimes, that's what being positive is.

386
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:49,000
It's not managing to turn every difficulty into happiness.

387
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,270
Nor is it looking for a lesson in

388
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:53,000
every painful moment.

389
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Some things are simply hard.

390
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Some disappointments take time.

391
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:03,000
And some days have no immediate solution.

392
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,000
But even in those moments,

393
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,390
we can try not to add extra

394
00:17:07,390 --> 00:17:10,110
pain by criticising ourselves.

395
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:12,000
You don't need to tell yourself:

396
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
"I should be happier."

397
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,000
You can simply admit:

398
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,000
"Today is hard."

399
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:24,090
And sometimes add: "I'm going to take care of myself

400
00:17:24,090 --> 00:17:26,000
as best I can."

401
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:29,320
You see, there's a difference between a positive

402
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:33,000
person and a person who refuses to see problems.

403
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:36,000
A positive person can accept reality.

404
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,000
She can cry.

405
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,200
She can ask for help.

406
00:17:39,250 --> 00:17:42,000
She can admit she doesn't know what to do.

407
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,740
But she tries not to turn a difficult

408
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:49,000
moment into a final verdict on her whole life.

409
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,000
One disappointment doesn't erase all your successes.

410
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:55,000
One mistake doesn't erase all your qualities.

411
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
One bad week doesn't erase all the good things

412
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
you've built.

413
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:05,000
And above all, your mood right now doesn't define your future.

414
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,120
I'd like you to imagine something.

415
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:10,910
You're looking at a photo of yourself taken

416
00:18:10,910 --> 00:18:12,000
five years ago.

417
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,430
That person may have had worries you

418
00:18:14,430 --> 00:18:16,000
no longer know today.

419
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,000
They had questions that have since found answers.

420
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:23,000
Maybe they were going through a hard time.

421
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
And yet, life went on.

422
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
You learned.

423
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:28,000
You changed.

424
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,790
You've lived moments that this older version

425
00:18:30,790 --> 00:18:34,140
of you couldn't even imagine.

426
00:18:34,190 --> 00:18:40,000
So why think today's difficulties will necessarily last forever?

427
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
You don't yet know the rest of your story.

428
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:47,070
And maybe that's reason enough to keep a

429
00:18:47,070 --> 00:18:49,000
little room for hope.

430
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,190
Before we end our conversation,

431
00:18:51,190 --> 00:18:55,000
I'd like to leave you with a simple thought.

432
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,200
You don't need to turn every day into

433
00:18:58,200 --> 00:19:01,090
an extraordinary day.

434
00:19:01,140 --> 00:19:04,000
You don't need to smile when you're sad.

435
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,620
You don't need to find a solution right away

436
00:19:07,620 --> 00:19:09,000
to all your problems.

437
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:12,380
And you certainly don't need to become a

438
00:19:12,380 --> 00:19:16,000
perfectly positive person.

439
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,320
You can simply learn to be a little

440
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:21,000
gentler with yourself.

441
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:25,000
To notice a small pleasant moment.

442
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:29,050
To question a thought that hurts you.

443
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:33,000
To protect your energy when you need to.

444
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,210
And to remind yourself that a hard moment doesn't

445
00:19:36,210 --> 00:19:38,000
tell your whole story.

446
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Maybe tomorrow will be a really beautiful day.

447
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Maybe it'll just be ordinary.

448
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,140
And maybe it'll be a bit complicated.

449
00:19:49,190 --> 00:19:51,360
But in each of these cases,

450
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:55,200
you can try to leave yourself a little room

451
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:59,000
to breathe, think and carry on.

452
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Thank you for spending this moment with me.

453
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
I hope these French words kept you gentle company,

454
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:09,000
and that this conversation gave you a little calm.

455
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:13,200
Before you go, I'd like to ask you a question.

456
00:20:13,250 --> 00:20:17,080
What little thing helps you smile again during

457
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,000
a hard day?

458
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,900
Is it a song, a walk,

459
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:26,000
a person, or just a few minutes of silence?

460
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,480
Tell me in the comments.

461
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:31,000
I'd be really happy to read you.

462
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
Take good care of yourself, my friend.

463
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
See you soon on Cozy French Radio.

464
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
See you very soon.
